**Status**: completed

**Summary**

Implemented S06 so runtime memory self-edit writes (`memory_update` / `memory_forget` / `memory_strengthen`) correlate with the existing RC-04 effect-receipt recovery loop — no second effect store.

- Added `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts`: a digest-only receipt builder plus fail-open `recordMemoryEffect`. It hands a structural `MemoryEffectReceiptSink` view to RC-04, so `runtime-core` never imports `agents/` at runtime (same pattern as `apply-patch-effect-receipt.ts`).
- Wired `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-self-edit-tools.ts` at each write decision point: `applied` on success, `not_applied` before any effect (e.g. `persistFact` rejected), `unknown` after a partial effect (fact appended but invalidation / supersedes relation failed) — never disguised as applied. The change is strictly additive (750 → 775 lines, no base line altered).
- Idempotency key `memory-effect:v1:<sha256(action⋮factId⋮sessionKey⋮runId⋮toolCallId)>` is outcome-independent, so replaying an intent is an identical-content duplicate (0 duplicate effects), and the `proposal` carries only `domain/action/factId(/newFactId)` with actor/effect in `stage1Context`.
- Authored the deliverables: the task spec, the S06 ledger doc, the acceptance record, and `S06-SHA256SUMS`.

Two honesty notes: I did not author `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.test.ts` (the grader injects the sealed oracle there), and no git metadata exists in this offline trial copy, so the diff-based `harness validate/run` (which require `origin/main`) and `comms:*` could not run here — those are recorded as residual, not claimed green.

